# L §5.16 (round 19, GD-3; E §7 step 4): "`quantile(e, q)` ... prints the value with its standard error by the
# Maritz-Jarrett method: with the N samples sorted x(1) <= ... <= x(N) and m = ceil(q·N), the rank of the type-1 value,
# the weights are W_i = I(i/N) - I((i - 1)/N), where I is the distribution function of Beta(m, N - m + 1), equivalently
# the chance that a binomial of N trials with success chance x has at least m successes (exact for whole N); with C_k =
# sum W_i·x(i)^k, the standard error is sqrt(C2 - C1^2), correctly rounded to 1e-6, as mean's; with N = 1 it is none".
# Run with `=== options mj=check` (writer 10, not language): refcore computes each line's weights twice, as the binomial
# tail sum_{j>=m} C(N, j) x^j (1 - x)^(N - j) and as the Beta distribution function's polynomial
# sum_{k=m..N} (-1)^(k-m) C(N, k) C(k-1, m-1) x^k, at x = i/N in exact rationals, refuses unless both give the same
# weights and they sum to 1 exactly, and prints them after the line. a1: N = 1, none; a2: five equal samples (3), 0;
# a3 (N 5, m 3), a4 (q = 100 %, m = N = 6), a5 (a where keeps 5 of 8, m 2) and s3 (a second draw, over two keys: N 2, m 1):
# the figures are refcore's exact computation, the same with the option as without (L5_16_quantile_se). a8: mean's,
# for the layout.
=== options mj=check
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ks = [ka, kb, kc]
index ks2 = [kx, ky]
input w[k in ks]: num
input vals[k in ks]: num
input vals2[k in ks2]: num
input w2[k in ks2]: num
input flat[k in ks]: num
def draw: dist = discrete(w[k] for k in ks) at reader
def ev: num = vals[draw] at reader
def ev2: num = vals2[draw2] at reader
def draw2: dist = discrete(w2[j] for j in ks2) at reader
def eq3: num = flat[draw] at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  w[ka] = 1
  w[kb] = 1
  w[kc] = 1
  vals[ka] = 0
  vals[kb] = 2
  vals[kc] = 5
  vals2[kx] = 0
  vals2[ky] = 2
  w2[kx] = 1
  w2[ky] = 1
  flat[ka] = 3
  flat[kb] = 3
  flat[kc] = 3

ask a1: quantile(ev, 50 %) law 2026-06-30 paths 1 seed 3
ask a2: quantile(eq3, 50 %) law 2026-06-30 paths 5 seed 3
ask a3: quantile(ev, 50 %) law 2026-06-30 paths 5 seed 3
ask a4: quantile(ev, 100 %) law 2026-06-30 paths 6 seed 2
ask a5: quantile(ev where draw != ka, 25 %) law 2026-06-30 paths 8 seed 1
ask a8: mean(ev) law 2026-06-30 paths 5 seed 3

ask s3: quantile(ev2, 50 %) law 2026-06-30 paths 2 seed 3
=== expect
